{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question","id":1076811,"title":"A hypothetical soul question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-11T22:29:21-07:00","id":1076811,"title":"A hypothetical soul question","content":"So, suppose I'm a Master of Death. <br /> <br /> I take a sleeper, remove their soul, put it in a soul jar. Then I take a mage, remove their soul, put it in a soul jar. Then I swap the souls.<br /> <br /> Now, we know being a mage is at least somewhat connected to the soul being altered in some way. So what happens? does the sleeper Awaken? Do they immediately jump to the original mages level? Become a sleepwalker? Stay asleep but gain some weird powers? See the supernal without an awakened soul to process it? And what happens to the mage? Do they unawaken (yes, we know what happens to a mage with <i>no</i> soul, but this is a mage with a <i>sleeper's</i> soul)? Involuntarily become a lich? Switch paths to whatever the sleeper would have awakened as?<br /> <br /> Or am I missing something and the actual answer is boring?<br /> <br /> (this just leads to other various questions- if I put a soul into a promethean, do they instantly undergo the new dawn? If I put a soul into a vampire, can they start feeling real emotions again? If I put a soul into a mummy, how many pieces will they find me in?- but that is perhaps getting away from my original question so hey)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T22:38:50-07:00","id":1076813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question#post1076811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I put a soul into a vampire, can they start feeling real emotions again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires still have their souls, so the beast will probably just claim the new soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T22:48:56-07:00","id":1076817,"title":"","content":"Humans with Awakened souls put into them might become Sleepwalkers, but this is never guaranteed. They may or may not have a better chance of Awakening in the future. Mages with Sleeper souls put into them slowly recover their Awakened might that they lost while soulless. Emphasis on 'slowly.'<br /> <br /> Of course, this is assuming that it's &quot;only&quot; the soul you're transplanting. There is an underlying assumption that while the numinous organ the Death Arcanum governs over is the soul as mages know it, there is more to the issue. Gnosis, for example, is often described as a &quot;vessel&quot; that contains and shapes the soul. (Or a scar that mutilates it, as some Banishers may claim)<br /> <br /> And then there are Reaper (and Lich) Legacies, whose Attainments may have stranger effects on the victims of soul theft and the stolen souls' recipients.<br /> <br /> All of these might be a topic for later supplements, maybe Signs of Sorcery if they find the space. Interaction with other supernaturals will likely be covered in the upcoming Crossover Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Until then, my personal taste is to have Prometheans not suffer Disquiet or Torment with a soul in them... but every time they would provoke either, it provokes Dissonance to erode the soul-binding spell and Quiescence to gaslight Sleepers. Vampires do feel emotions. It's just that predatory and survival-instinct ones overshadow them in most cases, and the long nights may leave them jaded to the human experience. Maybe the Beast inside them is tamer while the soul is bound on them, or the Beast gobbles up the new soul. Mummies already have souls, albeit fragmented and liquified. They call them Pillars. Putting another soul in them will be exactly like having two souls, which doesn't do a thing as far as I know. Unless the mage breaks the soul down into Pillars before grafting them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:03:40-07:00","id":1076819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question#post1076811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or am I missing something and the actual answer is boring?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's the answer. Souls can be swapped as you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (this just leads to other various questions- if I put a soul into a promethean, do they instantly undergo the new dawn? </div> </div> </div>No. You probably can't attach it in a useful way. It's likely the equivelant of a walking soul jar. Also, the New Dawn is a bit more involved than simply having a soul, it also includes rewriting reality on a fairly major scale which simply attaching a soul probably wouldn't do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I put a soul into a vampire, can they start feeling real emotions again? </div> </div> </div>They already feel real emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:09:56-07:00","id":1076820,"title":"","content":"So, it seems the answer is &quot;Nor very much happens, really&quot;?<br /> <br /> Ok, I will look forward to the crossover chronicles and until then feel vaguely sad my mage can't fix all the World Of Darkness' problems by just relocating people's souls willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> (Also I may have missed a change between first ed and second ed vampire, oops)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:28:26-07:00","id":1076825,"title":"","content":"A mage can't solve the world's problems, but he sure can solve his ones. Or those of his friends. One of Mage's themes is, after all, having power/knowledge and what to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T00:18:06-07:00","id":1076841,"title":"","content":"I thought that putting a soul into a Promethean results in a firestorm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:35:31-07:00","id":1076904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1076841#post1076841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that putting a soul into a Promethean results in a firestorm...</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:34:23-07:00","id":1076933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1076813#post1076813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires still have their souls</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they? If we're using what Mages call souls as the baseline, that vanishes the instant someone dies, and vampires who are raised long after their death - be it by Embracing a corpse or a Strix having a laugh - don't differ in any noticeable way from any other vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:43:30-07:00","id":1076934,"title":"","content":"They do.<br /> <br /> If it ever left, vampire magic brings it back.<br /> <br /> Mages able to do such things would be able to see that a vampire has its soul as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:50:53-07:00","id":1076940,"title":"","content":"Related- is there any mechanical effect at all to having a soul that isn't yours? Or will any soul do?<br /> While it would probably be waiting for the crossover chronicle- just in case, are there any rules or hints on what happens if you give a sleeper a soul tainted by the supernatural (a vampires, a changeling?) or that strictly speaking isn't human at all (a werewolf's, a beast's?)<br /> <br /> (i would assume that &quot;Sever the awakened soul&quot; can do other supernatural's souls)<br /> <br /> For that matter, do animals have souls? <br /> <br /> (Also, I am starting to look alarmingly like a reaper trying to crowd-source their Legacy, there's an arguably even worse story idea then the soul switching one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:55:23-07:00","id":1076942,"title":"","content":"It depends on the soul and how it's done.<br /> <br /> When an idigam rips the soul out of you, they can put a spirit in its place, making a Claimed. They could also put another soul in its place, and give the person a Persistent Madness Condition.<br /> <br /> It might be in the crossover chronicle, but it might appear in their own books. Souls aren't solely the domain of mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:01:25-07:00","id":1076946,"title":"","content":"The answer's a resounding &quot;Maybe&quot;. There's no mechanical guidelines on the effects of having a new soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1076934#post1076934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do.<br /> <br /> If it ever left, vampire magic brings it back.<br /> <br /> Mages able to do such things would be able to see that a vampire has its soul as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? Isn't it supposed to be one of the big questions of the setting? Aren't vampires meant to be left questioning if they're the same person or just a good simulacrum?<br /> <br /> I mean, a reaper could outright steal someone's soul, then let a vampire turn them, just to see the effects. That's a very Ordo Dracul thing to do.<br /> <br /> Guess it's something that'll get answered in the Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:25:45-07:00","id":1076955,"title":"","content":"Vampires probably have something that fills their soul slot (see VtR 2E's section on Diablerie), but whatever they have (whether it's their original soul but changed, or something new altogether) is very different from a normal human soul.<br /> <br /> Mages are the only supernaturals that have souls close enough to human souls that they can be &quot;easily&quot; swapped with no lasting consequences if done correctly. Other soul equivalents has no rules for soul swapping yet, but if it's possible it'd probably have major consequences for both donor and recipient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:06:53-07:00","id":1076977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1076946#post1076946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it? Isn't it supposed to be one of the big questions of the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> From first edition's core book on, there's been no question that vampires in Requiem have souls. It's constantly remarked upon from an in-world view and out, there's many abilities that shape or alter their souls, and abilities that allow them to work with the souls of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aren't vampires meant to be left questioning if they're the same person or just a good simulacrum? </div> </div> </div>No. That was a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire\">possible alternative brought up by someone who didn't like the idea that people would choose to become a vampire</a>. If the game is about questioning anything, it would be their humanity. The existence of their soul is not in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:27:09-07:00","id":1077171,"title":"","content":"They might have &quot;souls&quot;, but do they have them in the sense Mages mean them? Because those are pretty different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:31:24-07:00","id":1077175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077171#post1077171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might have &quot;souls&quot;, but do they have them in the sense Mages mean them? Because those are pretty different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their 'detect soul' powers can see them, though they'd probably notice something's off about them. They can use magic to deal with them. I'm not sure what other sense they'd use the term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:42:25-07:00","id":1077186,"title":"","content":"Can you give any examples of that? I haven't seen anything in the core book about being able to see souls of other supers or being able to manipulate them. Or is it a 1E thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:58:00-07:00","id":1077195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077186#post1077186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give any examples of that? I haven't seen anything in the core book about being able to see souls of other supers or being able to manipulate them. Or is it a 1E thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a first edition thing, but there's no exception in the abilities that notice or affect souls that they must be ordinary human souls. Likely any specific details are waiting for the Crossover book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=944789#post944789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for a long time now, I've been blowing off crossover mechanical queries like &quot;so what happens when vampires feed from mages&quot; or &quot;what does Infrastructure look like under Mage Sight&quot; or &quot;What's the Hedge in Mage cosmology&quot; because I wanted a writer to be paid for it.<br /> <br /> It's also because I knew this was coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:24:31-07:00","id":1077219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was a 1e thing with Aura Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:28:02-07:00","id":1077224,"title":"","content":"At the very least, their 'Souls' are no longer connected to the Temenos though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:39:08-07:00","id":1077390,"title":"","content":"This topic has been discussed around before. Demons, Sin Eaters, and Prometheans don't have souls. Many inhuman characters do have souls, inhuman souls. Vampires have vampire souls and while it seems like someone does know what that means it isn't common knowledge. Souls disappear when a human dies and vampires must die before they become vampires. Some vampires are dead long enough we can say there is no chance the human soul remains. When a dead body becomes a vampire, a soul is generated. The rest is a mystery. A person that has their soul removed is still the same person by most standards so a vampire can be the same person, dead and soul gone, with a new soul. A similar process would occur for a Sin Eater except they have a Geist that would take care of the soulless issue. Beasts are even stranger as their soul is some nightmare monster that lives in a dream realm. The question is interesting but the answer is complicated and has not been covered so far. I expect that to change at some point when an appropriate space opens up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:48:52-07:00","id":1077448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077390#post1077390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic has been discussed around before. Demons, Sin Eaters, and Prometheans don't have souls. Many inhuman characters do have souls, inhuman souls. Vampires have vampire souls and while it seems like someone does know what that means it isn't common knowledge. Souls disappear when a human dies and vampires must die before they become vampires. Some vampires are dead long enough we can say there is no chance the human soul remains. When a dead body becomes a vampire, a soul is generated. The rest is a mystery. A person that has their soul removed is still the same person by most standards so a vampire can be the same person, dead and soul gone, with a new soul. A similar process would occur for a Sin Eater except they have a Geist that would take care of the soulless issue. Beasts are even stranger as their soul is some nightmare monster that lives in a dream realm. The question is interesting but the answer is complicated and has not been covered so far. I expect that to change at some point when an appropriate space opens up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Beast the soul itself? I might be wrong but I kinda thought that a vampire soul was, in fact, the beast--and had something to do with the Strix, how much, was up to the ST, but it was food for thought.<br /> <br /> I think Sin-Eaters would have some kind of soul, albeit different. It's kind of a true resurrection. I can't wait for 2E to come out uuuugh its going to be a painful wait. But just this last week I think I saw on the forums people make compelling arguments for sin-eaters having souls and sin-eaters not having souls. It's just a strange situation cuz they're also claimed but not claimed...<br /> <br /> Demons and Proms, right on the money though, for certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:08:13-07:00","id":1077458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077448#post1077448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Beast the soul itself? I might be wrong but I kinda thought that a vampire soul was, in fact, the beast--and had something to do with the Strix, how much, was up to the ST, but it was food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the belief of Belial's Brood, they believe the 'vampire's soul' was gifted to them by the Adversary and getting in tune with it requires an abandonment of Humanity. Some do anyways.<br /> <br /> In most cases the Beast is described as part of or within the vampire's soul. I'd imagine that the rest is full of their vestiges of Humanity but there's likely more to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:16:34-07:00","id":1077468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077448#post1077448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the Beast the soul itself? I might be wrong but I kinda thought that a vampire soul was, in fact, the beast--and had something to do with the Strix, how much, was up to the ST, but it was food for thought.<br /> <br /> I think Sin-Eaters would have some kind of soul, albeit different. It's kind of a true resurrection. I can't wait for 2E to come out uuuugh its going to be a painful wait. But just this last week I think I saw on the forums people make compelling arguments for sin-eaters having souls and sin-eaters not having souls. It's just a strange situation cuz they're also claimed but not claimed...<br /> <br /> Demons and Proms, right on the money though, for certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationship between whatever it is vampires have for a soul (and devour in diablerie), and whatever the vampires' inner Beast really is, has not been confirmed yet. Likely a deliberate choice, both to keep the mysteries going on and because themes of Vampire are largely about what you are doing tonight, right here and right now.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters on the other hand... in 2e, <i>sin-eaters don't have a soul</i>. At least that's what the developer for it said <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042273#post1042273\">here</a>. And if you think about it, its less a setting change and more like a logical conclusion that nobody noticed until now. The Bound are people who have, right before their Bargain. truly died. The soul disappears when you die. Therefore, the soul of the to-be-Bound is already gone when he makes the Bargain. However, the Bound obviously don't seem to suffer from soul loss. It's likely that the geist is substituting for the soul, so all soul-affecting powers would be directed towards the geist. Seeing how Beasts no-sell most soul-affecting powers thanks to their soul being their Horror, an Astral monstrosity, the Bound also likely no-sell most soul-affecting powers. (Exceptions are rather powerful feats of magic, like that 5-dot mage spell that allows you to rip out souls)<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Bound are not Claimed. The developers also said that geist-Claimed exist as a separate class of beings. Not that the local Spirit mage or Storm Lord werewolf would realize that, without getting a super-close look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:29:51-07:00","id":1077475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077468#post1077468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The relationship between whatever it is vampires have for a soul (and devour in diablerie), and whatever the vampires' inner Beast really is, has not been confirmed yet. Likely a deliberate choice, both to keep the mysteries going on and because themes of Vampire are largely about what you are doing tonight, right here and right now.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters on the other hand... in 2e, <i>sin-eaters don't have a soul</i>. At least that's what the developer for it said <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042273#post1042273\">here</a>. And if you think about it, its less a setting change and more like a logical conclusion that nobody noticed until now. The Bound are people who have, right before their Bargain. truly died. The soul disappears when you die. Therefore, the soul of the to-be-Bound is already gone when he makes the Bargain. However, the Bound obviously don't seem to suffer from soul loss. It's likely that the geist is substituting for the soul, so all soul-affecting powers would be directed towards the geist. Seeing how Beasts no-sell most soul-affecting powers thanks to their soul being their Horror, an Astral monstrosity, the Bound also likely no-sell most soul-affecting powers. (Exceptions are rather powerful feats of magic, like that 5-dot mage spell that allows you to rip out souls)<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Bound are not Claimed. The developers also said that geist-Claimed exist as a separate class of beings. Not that the local Spirit mage or Storm Lord werewolf would realize that, without getting a super-close look.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even if they could, they might not choose to believe it. A woof might just say you are arguing semantics no matter the proof. Thanks for the clear-up though! I knew their soul departs after death but I thought that the Bargain might include some clause of bringing the soul back, and that would be why the bargain manifestation was so powerful, but I guess not, and that's fine.<br /> <br /> As for Giest claimed, I saw that earlier today, but I thought that was still kinda up in the air? It would be quite a damper if it gets changed out last-second for the full release of 2E Giest, but that's future-me's problem.<br /> <br /> Is it me or are vampire's the least cosmic of the splats? I kinda like the idea that they, in exchange, get the most mysterious existence. Most down-to-earth splat gets the most mysterious and confounding ontology? That sorta thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:36:50-07:00","id":1077478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077475#post1077475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if they could, they might not choose to believe it. A woof might just say you are arguing semantics no matter the proof.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my viewpoint. They're not Claimed as in the Manifestation, but it's similar enough that it might as well be lumped in, just like Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it me or are vampire's the least cosmic of the splats? I kinda like the idea that they, in exchange, get the most mysterious existence. Most down-to-earth splat gets the most mysterious and confounding ontology? That sorta thing? </div> </div> </div>They do seem that way. Very old vampires tend to have a lot of power but even then most of it is terrestrial. We should be seeing more of that with the new elder book. And potentially with the crossover book. It doesn't help that really delving into other worlds would require other books, something much of Chronicles has avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:37:35-07:00","id":1077479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077475#post1077475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are vampire's the least cosmic of the splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the most evident case of convergent evolution among the major strains of magical being and their particular metaphysics facilitate their being the bleeding edge of supernatural adaptations, particularly vis-a-vis curses and such.<br /> <br /> Vampires come from all over and stretch in all different directions, which works best with a grounding in a world of flesh touched by soul-eating horrors from the endless dark.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(We fight the hydra.)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:42:29-07:00","id":1077480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077479#post1077479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're the most evident case of convergent evolution among the major strains of magical being and their particular metaphysics facilitate their being the bleeding edge of supernatural adaptations, particularly vis-a-vis curses and such.<br /> <br /> Vampires come from all over and stretch in all different directions, which works best with a grounding in a world of flesh touched by soul-eating horrors from the endless dark.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(We fight the hydra.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>from the endless dark? you're not suggesting the abyss are you? Or is that just sort of a general statement on theme instead of, uh, something more specific? I'm being distracted by the fact that Endless Dark is a chapter title in Summoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:53:20-07:00","id":1077487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077480#post1077480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> from the endless dark? you're not suggesting the abyss are you? Or is that just sort of a general statement on theme instead of, uh, something more specific? I'm being distracted by the fact that Endless Dark is a chapter title in Summoners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably general statement, although I can see at least one strain of Kindred being Abyssal in origin, due to there being hundreds of them. (Convergent evolution, and all that)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:57:21-07:00","id":1077488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077480#post1077480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">from the endless dark? you're not suggesting the abyss are you?</div> </div> </div> </div>General statement with a very loose specific core of Strixworld(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:58:50-07:00","id":1077490,"title":"","content":"StrixWorld is my favourite theme park!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:59:07-07:00","id":1077491,"title":"","content":"You could probably argue that everything that isn't evident in our world is the result of some Abyssal incursion that's managed to glom onto the Fallen World. It probably wouldn't be that hard, though the disagreements would be numerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:00:51-07:00","id":1077492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077490#post1077490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">StrixWorld is my favourite theme park!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've decided you're my favorite person","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:02:50-07:00","id":1077493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077490#post1077490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">StrixWorld is my favourite theme park!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, but all it has are horror houses!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:44:17-07:00","id":1077577,"title":"","content":"Its a 1e source, and your obviously welcome to ignore it as you fancy, but I think Tome of Mysteries had a section where it was pretty definitive on the issue of Mage Magic vs Vampire Souls. Basically the two are oil and water and dont mix, a mage can not easily verify if the soul exists, nor can he manipulate it with standard spells.<br /> <br /> Here is the passage.<br /> &quot;A willworker cannot interact with the soul of a vampire (if indeed such creatures still possess souls; Death and Spirit Arcana perceptions always reveal inconclusive information when used in an attempt to discern whether or not Kindred are ensouled beings). Likewise, the Awakened have no power to do anything to the soul of a werewolf.&quot;<br /> <br /> After mulling it over I am happy with this interpretation, as it leaves the question of whether a Vampire has a soul (as a Mage would understand it) as a great mystery for a PC to Obsess over. I could see this as a good example of the type of knowledge a Mage might conjure a powerful Spectre to uncover, or might spur him to dive into the Temenos to question Death herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:37:00-07:00","id":1078077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1077577#post1077577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After mulling it over I am happy with this interpretation, as it leaves the question of whether a Vampire has a soul (as a Mage would understand it) as a great mystery for a PC to Obsess over. I could see this as a good example of the type of knowledge a Mage might conjure a powerful Spectre to uncover, or might spur him to dive into the Temenos to question Death herself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember the last time soul obsessed mages dealt with vampires? What is the worst that can happen right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13276-bristark","name":"Bristark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13276_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:41:53-07:00","id":1078419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bristark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1078077#post1078077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Remember the last time soul obsessed mages dealt with vampires? What is the worst that can happen right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am sure everything will be fine! The average PC is so Wise after all, no chance they might make any perilous or rash decisions with potentially disastrous consequences. No chance at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:54:13-07:00","id":1078423,"title":"","content":"So, what I'm getting is that my Mage character should definitely be a Reaper trying to figure out how to interact with other supernatural's soul-equivalents, so they can pull them out and screw around with them, secure in the knowledge that there is no way bad things could occur in any way as a result? Huzzah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:31:31-07:00","id":1078435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076811-a-hypothetical-soul-question?p=1078423#post1078423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what I'm getting is that my Mage character should definitely be a Reaper trying to figure out how to interact with other supernatural's soul-equivalents, so they can pull them out and screw around with them, secure in the knowledge that there is no way bad things could occur in any way as a result? Huzzah!</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally i would work with your ST and craft a story wherein you first are obsessed with the the nature of souls, and then eventually that obsession gets you targeted by one of the reaper legacies, and then you end up joining one. There are a number of neat reaper legacies so at least one will likely fit a character that you build.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13276-bristark","name":"Bristark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13276_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:51:07-07:00","id":1078484,"title":"","content":"I will do this! I look forward to becoming an entry in someone else's Night Horrors book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}